Notes:

- Only the modules that public/sw.js uses are included, in production builds
  (.prod.js). Source maps are omitted. Adding a new workbox.* module to sw.js
  requires copying its .prod.js file here as well; otherwise the service
  worker fails to install.
- sw.js must call workbox.setConfig({ modulePathPrefix: "/workbox-v7.3.0/",
  debug: false }) before touching any workbox.* module. Without the prefix
  workbox-sw.js falls back to its built-in CDN URL; without debug: false it
  requests .dev.js builds on localhost, which are not shipped.
- The module builds in the 7.3.0 packages carry the internal marker
  "workbox:<module>:7.2.0". This is how upstream published them; the files
  are unchanged.
- Upgrading: create a new versioned directory (workbox-vX.Y.Z), update
  importScripts and modulePathPrefix in sw.js, bump CACHE_VERSION and
  refresh the checksums above.
